Package: rhoGE
Type: Package
Title: Expression-Effect Genetic Correlation Between Two Traits
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person("Jianhai", "Chen", email = "jianhaic@uci.edu", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Estimates the expression-effect genetic correlation (rho_GE) between any two
    traits from GWAS summary statistics. For each gene and tissue, cis-eQTLs are used as
    instruments and the effects of genetically regulated expression on both traits are
    estimated jointly with FusioMR; tissue-level evidence is combined per gene with the
    aggregated Cauchy association test, and rho_GE is the correlation of the gene-level
    effects across genes. Genes are also classified into the four directional classes
    (d+f+, d+f-, d-f+, d-f-) that distinguish antagonistic from synergistic pleiotropy.
License: MIT + file LICENSE
Encoding: UTF-8
Depends: R (>= 4.0.0)
Imports: data.table, stats, FusioMR (>= 2.0.0)
